TEXT -96 -200 Left 3 ;#55 Parallel LC circuit frequency sweep
TEXT -96 -144 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hqhV50852jA
TEXT -96 -104 Left 2 ;An AC sweep from 5 kHz to 200 kHz of the same parallel tank and generator.
TEXT -96 -72 Left 2 ;The tank voltage and impedance peak at resonance; below it the tank is inductive, above it capacitive.
TEXT 640 16 Left 2 ;CH1: voltage across the L1 || C1 tank (Alan's channel 1).  V1: 4 V p-p open circuit, Rser = 50 ohm generator output.
TEXT 640 48 Left 2 ;Assumed (not stated in the video): L1 = 220 uH with 1 ohm winding resistance, C1 = 100 nF, so f0 = 33.9 kHz.
TEXT 640 128 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 5k 200k
TEXT 640 168 Left 2 !.meas ac F_RES WHEN im(V(ch1)/I(V1))=0
TEXT 640 208 Left 2 !.meas ac Z_RES FIND mag(V(ch1)/I(V1)) WHEN im(V(ch1)/I(V1))=0
TEXT 640 248 Left 2 !.meas ac TANK_RES FIND mag(V(ch1)) WHEN im(V(ch1)/I(V1))=0
